refentry.refsect1:
&reftitle.errors;


 Throws RdKafka\Exception with the error returned by librdkafka, for example after a fatal error, once the consumer has been closed and released.



 Throws RdKafka\Exception with code RD_KAFKA_RESP_ERR__STATE when called from one of the consumer's callbacks, or while another call to RdKafka\KafkaConsumer::close is still running. From a callback, record that the consumer should close, and close it after the method that invoked the callback returns.

&reftitle.changelog;







     &Version;
     &Description;





     7.0.0

      Close errors are thrown instead of ignored. Calling this method from a callback throws.
